{"uid":"bf2d39048fcce25c","name":"test_genuine_stagnation_guard_still_fails_job_unaffected","fullName":"tests.test_no_progress_instant_failures#test_genuine_stagnation_guard_still_fails_job_unaffected","historyId":"2b88f91ce4d17d6ca3f010cf1a19dd60","time":{"start":1791931391787,"stop":1791931395441,"duration":3654},"description":"Regression check: genuine no-progress (a worker that runs to\n    completion every time but never changes tasks.json -- no crash, no\n    instant exit) must still trip the ordinary 3-iterations-no-progress\n    guard exactly as before task 059 -- but task 012 (PRD requirement B.3,\n    #153) changed what tripping it means on the LAST approach (`max_\n    approaches=1` here, so every approach is the last one): the run now\n    pauses and escalates (`state: \"paused\"`, `pauseReason: \"stagnation\"`)\n    instead of exiting `failed` silently, so this waits for the pause\n    (bounded by `wait_state`'s own deadline) rather than for process exit,\n    which never happens on its own here. The pre-B.3 `verdict:\n    \"unverified\"` was written BY that `failed` ending, so its\n    current-behaviour counterpart is asserted here instead: a parked run\n    carries no settled verdict and its engine is still alive.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Regression check: genuine no-progress (a worker that runs to<br />\ncompletion every time but never changes tasks.json -- no crash, no<br />\ninstant exit) must still trip the ordinary 3-iterations-no-progress<br />\nguard exactly as before task 059 -- but task 012 (PRD requirement B.3,<br />\n#153) changed what tripping it means on the LAST approach (<code>max_ approaches=1</code> here, so every approach is the last one): the run now<br />\npauses and escalates (<code>state: &quot;paused&quot;</code>, <code>pauseReason: &quot;stagnation&quot;</code>)<br />\ninstead of exiting <code>failed</code> silently, so this waits for the pause<br />\n(bounded by <code>wait_state</code>'s own deadline) rather than for process exi